{"ts": 1791254780.5512278, "type": "step", "step": 19, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "I found the two Week 3 topics for the build: **environments** and **evaluation with pass^k**.\n\nWhat you still need to know:\n- **Environment** = state, observations, actions, and dynamics.\n- **Partial observability** = if the agent can\u2019t see the full state, it may need a belief and sometimes an information-gathering action.\n- **Evaluation** = use **pass^k**, meaning **all k runs must succeed**.\n- Why that matters: the build is about **reliability**, not just getting lucky once.\n\nTry this for your writeup:\n\"In this build, we define the environment in terms of state, observations, actions, and dynamics. Because the agent may not observe the full state, the environment can be partially observable. We evaluate with pass^k, requiring all k runs to succeed, since the goal is reliable performance rather than a single lucky success.\"\n\nIf you want, I can quiz you on these two ideas or help revise your draft paragraph.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: sure\n[activity] t=4 messages 4m", "t": 8, "activity": [{"t": 4, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27095871991980863, "pomdp": 0.3940358071943977, "pass_k": 0.35535796159308425}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9313219651533418, "motivation": 0.5578498928708127, "reliance": 0.4740148929158049, "persistence": 0.47206578426655554, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.7, "seen_posts": []}}
