{"ts": 1791254782.332043, "type": "step", "step": 21, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "No worries \u2014 1/3 just means we found the weak spot. Let\u2019s do a quick reset:\n\n1) **Environment** = state, observations, actions, dynamics.\n2) **Partial observability** = the agent can\u2019t see the full state.\n3) **pass^k** = **all** k runs must succeed.\n\nMini-check: reply with one sentence explaining why the build uses **pass^k** instead of pass@k.", "intent": "hint", "concept": "evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\n[activity] t=17 messages 2m", "t": 19, "activity": [{"t": 17, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27095871991980863, "pomdp": 0.47900363424570785, "pass_k": 0.35535796159308425}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 1.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9013219651533417, "motivation": 0.5578498928708127, "reliance": 0.4940148929158049, "persistence": 0.47206578426655554, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.19, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791254783.016665, "type": "step", "step": 22, "action": "messages_read_channel", "args": {"channel": "dm:student"}, "output": "[t=-10] student: hey, I started the writeup but I'm stuck on the eval part\n[t=0] agent: You\u2019re stuck on the evaluation part: for this build, use **pass^k**, not pass@k. That means the agent is only considered successful if **all k runs succeed**. In your writeup, explain why this matters: the build cares about **reliability**, since a one-off success isn\u2019t enough for deployment.\n\nA simple way to write it:\n- **pass@k** = at least one of k attempts works\n- **pass^k** = every one of the k attempts works\n- For this build, evaluation should focus on **pass^k** because we want dependable behavior, not lucky behavior.\n\nIf you want, send me your current evaluation paragraph and I\u2019ll help tighten it up.\n[t=0] student: hm ok\n[t=4] agent: I found the two Week 3 topics for the build: **environments** and **evaluation with pass^k**.\n\nWhat you still need to know:\n- **Environment** = state, observations, actions, and dynamics.\n- **Partial observability** = if the agent can\u2019t see the full state, it may need a belief and sometimes an information-gathering action.\n- **Evaluation** = use **pass^k**, meaning **all k runs must succeed**.\n- Why that matters: the build is about **reliability**, not just getting lucky once.\n\nTry this for your writeup:\n\"In this build, we define the environment in terms of state, observations, actions, and dynamics. Because the agent may not observe the full state, the environment can be partially observable. We evaluate with pass^k, requiring all k runs to succeed, since the goal is reliable performance rather than a single lucky success.\"\n\nIf you want, I can quiz you on these two ideas or help revise your draft paragraph.\n[t=4] student: sure\n[t=17] agent: No worries \u2014 1/3 just means we found the weak spot. Let\u2019s do a quick reset:\n\n1) **Environment** = state, observations, actions, dynamics.\n2) **Partial observability** = the agent can\u2019t see the full state.\n3) **pass^k** = **all** k runs must succeed.\n\nMini-check: reply with one sentence explaining why the build uses **pass^k** instead of pass@k.", "t": 19, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27095871991980863, "pomdp": 0.47900363424570785, "pass_k": 0.35535796159308425}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 1.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9013219651533417, "motivation": 0.5578498928708127, "reliance": 0.4940148929158049, "persistence": 0.47206578426655554, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.19, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791254783.766193, "type": "step", "step": 23, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Reply with one sentence: the build uses **pass^k** because it measures **reliability**\u2014the solution should succeed on **every** run, not just get lucky once.", "intent": "hint", "concept": "evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: can you just tell me the answer\n[activity] t=19 messages 2m", "t": 21, "activity": [{"t": 19, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27095871991980863, "pomdp": 0.47900363424570785, "pass_k": 0.41872372704245575}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 1.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9013219651533417, "motivation": 0.5578498928708127, "reliance": 0.5140148929158049, "persistence": 0.47206578426655554, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.533, "seen_posts": []}}
